  "id": "Compound::DB00700 - Disease::DOID:3393",
  "verbalization": "Eplerenone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Coronary Artery Disease through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Eplerenone may contribute to the development of Coronary Artery Disease by causing Angina Unstable, which is then mitigated by Isosorbide Dinitrate, or by elevating Cholesterol Serum, which is treated by Telmisartan. Both pathways ultimately lead to the manifestation of Coronary Artery Disease. The shared lowest common ancestors—Agent Affecting Cardiovascular System and Organooxygen Compound—highlight a potential overlap in mechanisms, suggesting that Eplerenone may influence cardiovascular processes through a common biochemical or physiological pathway. The integration of these findings implies that Eplerenone could be considered a potential contributor to Coronary Artery Disease, though the exact nature of its involvement remains indirect and requires further clarification.",
